__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository holds CODE. Observations and fit products stay out of it.
#
# Both are reproducible from what IS tracked: the staged FITS come from the
# SAPPHIRES EDR release, and every result is regenerable from a config plus
# `python -m dingo.run <ID>`. The config is the artifact worth versioning -- it
# is the thing that records what was fitted and why -- and dingo.catalogs
# generates configs from the catalogue, so the provenance chain is complete
# without committing a single byte of data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Staged cutouts (R/C grism + direct image per source). Configs are KEPT.
data/**/*.fits

# psf/webbPSF_F444W.fits IS tracked, deliberately, despite being a FITS file.
# It is a calibration input rather than an observation or a fit product, it is
# 743 KB, and without it a fresh clone cannot run the morphology fit at all.
# It previously lived in an old run's output directory, so archiving that run
# silently broke diagnostics/measure_inclination.py.

# Chains, checkpoints, derived posteriors, plots, run logs.
results/
logs/

# Superseded notebooks and a duplicate copy of the ID15665 cutouts.
Archive_6/

# Scratch output from the figure and map scripts.
maps/
*.log

# Superseded notebooks, kept on disk but out of the repo.
#   run_dingo_sample.ipynb  sampled inc_v free (no FIX_INCLINATION anywhere in
#                           it) and carried 13 MB of outputs, which contradicts
#                           the CODE-only rule above. kinematics.ipynb replaces it.
#   1-fit-kinematics.ipynb  the original Adam-only fit: no MCMC, no error bars,
#                           no rotation-vs-null test, so it could not report a
#                           non-detection.
run_dingo_sample.ipynb
1-fit-kinematics.ipynb
drizzle_utils.py
